# Frontmatter exemptions — read by tenet-audit/scripts/frontmatter-check.sh
# One shell glob per line, relative to the repo root. '*' crosses directories.
# Everything not listed here must carry title/type/status/updated.

# Claude Code owns this schema (name / description / allowed-tools), not ours.
# A SKILL.md that carried title/type/status/updated instead would not load.
skills/*/SKILL.md

# Skill reference files. They are read through a SKILL.md, never on their own, so
# repo-doc frontmatter would be four lines of noise in every model context that
# opens one.
skills/*/references/*.md

# The shipped vault skeleton. These files are copied into a user's vault by
# bootstrap.sh and then belong to that vault, which has its own frontmatter
# schema (type/created/status/scope) — not this repository's.
vault-template/*

# The README is the repository's front door, rendered by GitHub. A frontmatter
# block would show up as a table above the first heading.
README.md

# The changelog, rendered by GitHub next to the README. Same reason: a frontmatter
# block would render as a table above the first heading. Its own header states the
# schema it does follow — one entry per manifest version bump, no commit hashes.
CHANGELOG.md
